- Replace → with a non-classical implication and analyze impact on propagation.

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical application of 3-valued logic in policy-like constraints with a concrete propagation strategy.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic with On= T, Off= F, Unknown= U
- Implication semantics and unknown propagation
- Forward/backtracking CSP approach to avoid F states

## Code Example
```javascript
function kleeneVal(a,b){ // a,b in {T,F,U}
  if(a==="F") return "T";
  if(a==="T" && b==="F") return "F";
  if(a==="T" && b==="T") return "T";
  return "U";
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale to n services with a mix of constraints?
- What if cycles exist or new constraints are added dynamically?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to integrate 3-valued logic with cardinality constraints in a policy-like setting and to sketch a solver.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene three-valued logic
- Arc-consistency/backtracking with U
- Cardinality constraints and pruning

## Code Example
```javascript
// sketch for Kleene tri-valued ops
const order = {F:0, U:1, T:2};
function not(x){ return x==='T'?'F': x==='F'?'T':'U'; }
function or(a,b){ return order[a] > order[b]? a : b; }
function and(a,b){ return order[a] < order[b]? a : b; }
function implies(a,b){ return or(not(a), b); }
```

## Follow-up Questions
